' 4+1 Scenarios (+1) - Review My Pokédex (US05)
' Version 1.1 - 2026-10-20 - reflects the current working tree
' Shows how the Logical view (PokedexViewModel, PokemonRepository) supports the caught list: the list comes
' only from Room (works offline); PokeAPI is only used for the "Caught x / y" total, which is optional.
@startuml scenarios-my-pokedex
!include ../style.puml

title Scenario - review My Pokédex
autonumber

actor User
participant PokedexScreen
participant PokedexViewModel
participant PokemonRepository
database "Local Database" as LocalDb
participant PokeAPI <<external>>

User -> PokedexScreen : opens the Pokédex tab
PokedexScreen -> PokedexViewModel : observes caughtPokemons, total
PokedexViewModel -> PokemonRepository : getCaught()
PokemonRepository -> LocalDb : SELECT caught_pokemon
LocalDb --> PokedexViewModel : caught list (Room LiveData)
PokedexViewModel -> PokemonRepository : getSpeciesCount()
PokemonRepository -> PokeAPI : GET pokemon-species?limit=1
alt PokeAPI answers
    PokeAPI --> PokedexViewModel : count
    PokedexViewModel --> PokedexScreen : "Caught x / y" + grid
else unreachable
    PokedexViewModel --> PokedexScreen : "Caught x" + grid
end
User -> PokedexScreen : sorts by Date caught
PokedexScreen -> PokedexViewModel : onSortChange(DateCaught)
PokedexViewModel --> PokedexScreen : sorted by caughtAt, newest first
@enduml
